ise  once the levitation magic wears off  percival takes off in a sprint  and easily catches up to the horse and  carriage realizing that percival  probably shouldn't be messed with donnie  returns his stuff  that's when percival reveals that he is  looking for his father  ironside and that he needs help finding  him  the troop has no idea who ironside is  but they do agree to take percival to a  nearby village  in the hope that someone there might  know about  ironside on the way to the village the  members of the troop reveal that at some  point in the past  they all wanted to become holy knights  but  they failed they don't really possess  any strong  magic the only thing that their magic is  good for is performing  cheap tricks so they became street  performers  once percival and the troop reach the  village they are shocked to see that a  giant wolf  is rampaging around the village this  wolf has some sort of demon-esque  mark on its tail just like that blue  demon from god's finger  and i have to say that the art style of  this wolf really reminded me of kath  pauluk from the king of chaos arc in the  original manga  now obviously this wolf is nowhere near  as powerful as kath  palug and percival actually beats him  easily by [ __ ] slapping him right in  the face  once the wolf is defeated the  demon-esque mark disappears from its  tail  and percival is celebrated as a hero  it's worth mentioning that  when it looked like percival was in  trouble at the very beginning of this  short fight donnie actually stepped in  to help  percival at the expense of getting  injured so it seems that dony is a good  guy after all  he was just extremely jaded and  resentful after failing to get into the  holy knights  meanwhile that fox from earlier watched  as the entire fight against the wolf  unfolded  and through some sort of magic crystal  there was someone else  watching as well inside a castle  somewhere  a fully armored knight is impressed that  percival was able to d